{
  "meta": {
    "source": "LarderStyleExample.jpg",
    "imageSize": { "width": 3330, "height": 1202 },
    "scaleFactor": 2,
    "scaleFactorBasis": "Measured body-paragraph line box at 48px physical (baseline-to-baseline). At a 16px body / 1.5 line-height that is 24px CSS, giving 2x. Cross-checked against card avatars (~59px->30px) and the logo mark (~75px->38px).",
    "units": "css-px",
    "notes": [
      "All hex values are pixel-sampled with probe.py (color-at / palette); sizes are measured then divided by the 2x scale factor.",
      "Font families are visual guesses only. The type is a friendly rounded grotesque/geometric sans (heading is very heavy, almost 'black' weight). Verify the real stack — candidates: General Sans, Poppins, Cabinet Grotesk.",
      "Card header tint colors (pink/mint/peach) rotate per card; they are decorative image backgrounds, not a single theme token.",
      "Cards have no visible border — separation is a soft drop shadow on the cream background. Shadow offset/blur/opacity are approximated from the visible falloff and should be treated as best-effort.",
      "Only the resting/default state is visible for every component; hover/focus/active states are not in the screenshot (except the active nav tab, which shows an orange underline).",
      "h1 font-size (40px) is inferred from a ~20px x-height; it may be 40-44px.",
      "Avatar diameter (~30px) and card gap (~30px) were measured within a pixel or two and snapped."
    ]
  },
